      title: "Port Alder",
      content: "Port Alder sits on the east shore of Lake Michigan with about 6,500 residents. It began as a lumber port, became a fruit-shipping town and is now mostly a place where people fish, sail, ride dune buggies and commute to somewhere larger. It has two stoplights, one high school and no tolerance for being called quaint.",
